title: 'FRAME: preserve view functions and reject duplicate pallet indices'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Multiple `#[pallet::view_functions]` blocks now contribute all their functions to metadata
    and runtime dispatch in declaration order, instead of silently keeping only the last block.
    Generated view-function implementations require the combined bounds of `Config` and every
    view-function block. Rebuild the runtime and regenerate metadata bindings as needed.

    Repeated `#[runtime::pallet_index]` attributes on a pallet are now rejected, including when
    their values match. Keep exactly one attribute. Retain the last previously specified index
    to preserve the index used by the old macro and existing call/event encoding. No storage
    migration is required.
crates:
- name: frame-support-procedural
  bump: major
- name: frame-support
  bump: major
